EXT. MAPLE HOLLOW PARK - DAY

Ring light on a tripod. Phone on a gimbal. A fake-casual dance setup at the edge of the lawn.

Tessa, 17, hair in a claw clip, loads the screen. She taps the red button twice and checks her follower count like it might have changed.

ON PHONE: 41.2K followers. LIVE in 3...2...1

Cam, 17, stands behind the tripod pretending to adjust the light. He keeps looking at the tote bag at his feet.

TESSA
ok ok ok we're live. hi besties. today's trend is the sidewalk glide, pls do not judge us.

CAM
(low)
You said no one would be here.

TESSA
(through a smile)
that's a ring light, not a spotlight. chill.

She starts the dance. He joins, stiff, limbs all wrong. Across the lawn, a woman in a beige raincoat, dark glasses, newspaper folded under her arm, watches without blinking.

CAM
Who's that?

TESSA
Just some lady. keep going.

He does not keep going. He stops. She spins mid-move and collides with him.

TESSA (CONT'D)
bro. you're ruining the take.

CAM
She's been here since we got here. She's cop-energy.

TESSA
she's reading a newspaper, Cam. nobody reads newspapers. that's what makes her fake.

The woman folds the paper, tucks it away, and starts toward them. Slow. Not hurrying.

Tessa taps the screen. LIVE keeps running.

ON PHONE: 3,900 watching. chat is flying. "who is that" "behind u" "RUN"

TESSA (CONT'D)
(whispering)
it's not funny anymore.

CAM
It was never supposed to be.

THE FLASH MOB, twelve kids in matching hoodies who have been stretching by the fountain, break into a synced dance. Phones up. Music BLASTS from a speaker.

The woman stops, confused, swallowed by the crowd.

TESSA (CONT'D)
(grinning)
go go go!

He grabs the tote bag. She grabs the gimbal. They run for the gate, laughing, terrified, thumbs still on the screen.

ON PHONE: 12K watching. "WHERE ARE U GOING"

At the gate, the woman is already there. She lifts her sunglasses.

DETECTIVE MARA ROY
(calm)
Hi, Tessa. Hi, Cam. Mind if I ask what's in the bag?

He freezes. She freezes. The phone keeps filming.

TESSA
(very small)
it's just... props.

MARA
Mm. That's what the last two said.

She holds out her hand.
